{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the Toolbar departed-participant courtesy repair at 5c4ce6627ff3f2952d320332a332bcc40ff4d768 (request/toolbar-departed-courtesy, one commit on main c3169d83, pushed; Rests-On governing request 297205f8). Review against replacement request 15311 and current artifacts 15279, 15280 and 15281; the earlier request 15271 and artifacts 15268-15270 name the same unchanged head; not merged.\n\nWhat holds, verified on a detached checkout. Toolbar.tsx:118 computes mayComposeState once from the shared isLiveParticipant (authority.ts:67, projected participant role only, no prose or presence) and applies it to exactly the seven ordinary-state routes: deny and request accept, disagree, propose adoption and request review, mark done, needs work; the enumeration of onRoute call sites is complete at eight, and the eighth, own-author withdraw (:201), signs supersede and is correctly not guarded. Direct ratification (ratify yes :132, agree :142, report accept :185) keeps canRatify and mayRatify alone; signingRefusal at Thread.tsx:600 remains the final check. The guard fails closed and hides rather than disables, consistent with the withdraw and roster courtesy beside it. Mutation matrix: each of the seven routes has an individual red proof (inverting or removing its guard fails the named departed-viewer assertion; propose adoption and request review proved separately), forcing the predicate false fails eleven live-participant assertions, replacing membership with authorship fails the same, and gating withdraw fails two tests including the pre-existing publish-authority false-denial case. Embed: make ui reproduces the committed bundle byte for byte, make ui-check exits 0, index.html references exactly the committed assets, nothing references the deleted index-CWe_-agv. Gates: npm test 139/139, npm run build, make docs (fresh, 62 s), gofmt, go build, go vet, git diff --check clean, go test ./internal/service/... ok. authority.ts:19-38 now describes the post-change coverage accurately.\n\nTwo changes before approval.\n\n1. Two comments at this head still assert the gap the commit closed. ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx:64-70 says the seven Toolbar controls \"are still drawn without asking\" isLiveParticipant, an explicit cross-reference to the authority.ts list this commit changed; ui/test/signing-standing.test.mjs:198-201 says the seven affordances are offered \"with no membership test — that is deliberate\", stating the opposite design intent beside a test that still passes. Request 15250 asks that the authority comment describe the exact post-change coverage; the head updated one of the three sites. Both are one-line edits.\n\n2. The fixture edits removed the only red proofs that direct ratification is not gated. components.test.mjs:27-28 now gives ratifier() and bystander() the participant role and before-signing.test.mjs adds participant to five fixtures (:159, :169, :179, :185, :267); those edits were needed for the new guard, but no fixture can now witness a non-participant ratifier. Measured: gating agree on isLiveParticipant fails three tests at base c3169d83 and none at this head; gating ratify yes fails two at base and none here; gating report accept fails six at base and none here. Request 15250 forbids gating the direct ratify actions beyond mayRatify and request 15271 asks me to confirm it; the code complies, the proof no longer exists. Add one case: an actor holding the admitted role but not participant still sees agree (and ratify yes, and report accept) in the toolbar.\n\nRecorded, not blocking: the assertion messages at before-signing.test.mjs:164 and :175 (\"dissent needs no authority\") are now false since both fixtures hold participant; the same head carries two artifact sets, 15268-15270 (branch toolbar-departed-courtesy) and the cited 15279-15281 (branch toolbar-live-participant-current), all live at 5c4ce662 at the same paths, so this verdict binds the cited three and the merge must